# React components

- Check `src/components/` before creating UI. Generic, reusable pieces (Button, Input, Modal, Table, Spinner, EmptyState) live there; feature-specific ones in `src/features/<feature>/components/`.
- One component per file, kebab-case filename, PascalCase named export (`project-card.tsx` → `ProjectCard`).
- Keep components small and presentational. Move data fetching and state logic into hooks (`use-*.ts`); move pure helpers into `src/lib/`.
- Type props with an exported `interface XProps`. Extend native props for wrappers so they stay flexible:

```tsx
export interface ButtonProps extends ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'danger';
}

export function Button({ variant = 'primary', className, ...rest }: ButtonProps) {
  return <button className={`btn btn--${variant} ${className ?? ''}`} {...rest} />;
}
```

- Prefer composition (`children`, render slots) over boolean-flag explosions or copy-pasted variants.
- If similar JSX appears twice, extract a component; if similar stateful logic appears twice, extract a hook.
- Derive values during render instead of syncing them with `useEffect`. Use `useMemo`/`useCallback` only for measured cost or referential stability.
- Stable `key`s from data ids, never array indexes for dynamic lists.
- No API calls, `fetch`, or business rules inside presentational components.
